I checked each remaining one against the tree. Every one matches what
comparable ports do:

- The prebuilt web frontend from upstream's linux_amd64 tarball:
  www/grafana installs its public/ tree from its linux-amd64 tarball
  in the same way. net-mgmt/prometheus3 and net-mgmt/alertmanager
  fetch a prebuilt web UI asset.
- REINPLACE_CMD in post-patch for default paths is the most common
  approach among Go ports (about 55). irc/soju makes the same
  /var/lib to /var/db change. ldflags -X would not work here, because
  signoz's defaults are struct literals, not package variables.
- post-install appends the hashed web asset names to TMPPLIST with
  find, as www/grafana does.

One correction: v6 said the pnpm frontend build has no offline path in
the tree. That was wrong. Mk/Uses/npm.mk prefetches node_modules, and
www/remark42 builds a pnpm frontend that way. I kept the prebuilt
files, as grafana does, because building them adds Node and a large
node_modules distfile to every build. If you would rather the port
build the frontend, say so and v8 will.

v7 passed fetch, then an offline build with a read-only DISTDIR,
stage, check-plist, and a 30-second run without a panic. Lint is
clean. A poudriere build and aarch64 are not checked.

